From e27e66b5f9af53fa2fc9469a81a167d7a0d36fe4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 02:29:48 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 6/6] fix(fs-usage): skip nested linked worktrees and honor
 abort while measuring

Workspace usage walked every entry under the repository, including linked worktrees
nested inside it (e.g. <repo>/.claude/worktrees/*). Each of those is a workspace of
its own and measured separately, so the bytes were double-counted and the walk ran
twice over the biggest subtrees, pinning a core for the whole Workspaces tab visit.

Detect a nested linked worktree by its .git file (gitdir: .../worktrees/<name>) and
skip its contents; submodules and nested repositories remain part of the checkout.
Thread the AbortSignal through the walk so a cancelled measurement stops instead of
finishing in the background.

Refs generalaction/emdash#3262

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Lf1ZxTXikvVa7e1BpWKy1d
